On 25 Aug 2006 13:35:53 -0700, eXcel wrote:

>* silver saber
>Certainly useful in Gehennom against all the silver-hating stuff.
>However, barbarians can't enhance sabers beyond basic skill.

  Silver sabers do extra d20 damage vs silver haters.  That averages to
10.5 more damage.  So for maximum average damage silver saber is the
obvious choice.  Enchant it to +7.

  As for whether to #twoweapon or go with the extra 9 AC from a +7 elven
shield, let me put it this way.  Up to eight monsters can hit you at a
time.  #twoweaponing can only hit one monster at a time.  Extra AC will
help against all of the attacks.

  Another consideration is that once you wake Rodney you should RUN!,
not fight.  Extra AC is passive.  Using it doesn't burn up turns you
should be using to run.  

  On the Ascension Run don't fight if you can run.  Proper preparation
means always being able to run.


